WEBVTT

1
00:00:26.274 --> 00:00:27.662
Well, just great!

2
00:00:27.742 --> 00:00:32.216
No, not the presentation.
That's terrible. Some idiot just hit me.

3
00:00:33.294 --> 00:00:36.004
Do you realize how much
this is going to cost?

4
00:00:36.084 --> 00:00:39.786
Not in money, which
I have plenty of, but in...

5
00:00:41.356 --> 00:00:43.007
What the...

6
00:00:43.392 --> 00:00:46.127
Get away from me! Get away!

7
00:00:51.631 --> 00:00:53.867
Help me. Someone help!

8
00:00:56.369 --> 00:00:58.204
Stay away!

9
00:00:58.740 --> 00:01:00.493
What are you doing?

10
00:01:09.718 --> 00:01:10.852
Look out!

11
00:01:22.963 --> 00:01:26.267
Wonder Woman! Save me! Save me from them!

12
00:01:26.834 --> 00:01:28.707
- From whom?
- Demons.

13
00:01:28.787 --> 00:01:30.738
They're everywhere. Don't you see them?

14
00:01:40.981 --> 00:01:43.196
I see only one.

15
00:01:52.126 --> 00:01:54.528
I'll ask you one last time.

16
00:01:54.996 --> 00:01:57.231
What did you do with my family?

17
00:01:58.031 --> 00:02:00.932
Steven, it's me, Gloria!

18
00:02:01.349 --> 00:02:03.307
I'm your wife.

19
00:02:03.387 --> 00:02:05.475
These are our children.

20
00:02:07.340 --> 00:02:11.899
You're not my family!
You killed them, just like the others.

21
00:02:11.979 --> 00:02:14.248
Now it's your turn.

22
00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:23.244
- No one's dying here tonight.
- It's not me you should be stopping.

23
00:02:23.324 --> 00:02:25.994
It's them. Look at them!

24
00:02:28.996 --> 00:02:30.532
Look at them!

25
00:02:37.137 --> 00:02:41.644
It's just like the neighbors.
Go to my shed. You'll see I'm right!

26
00:02:59.693 --> 00:03:01.730
What have you done?

27
00:03:26.419 --> 00:03:28.257
Let me help you.

28
00:03:29.224 --> 00:03:31.245
It's not my fault.

29
00:03:31.325 --> 00:03:35.397
I've given birth to the devil.
It's the devil!

30
00:03:37.664 --> 00:03:39.954
You're tired. Give me the baby.

31
00:03:40.034 --> 00:03:42.271
You don't want to hurt her.

32
00:04:16.237 --> 00:04:18.056
I'm sorry.

33
00:04:46.166 --> 00:04:49.357
These crimes were committed
by law-abiding citizens.

34
00:04:49.437 --> 00:04:52.427
They all claim to have seen
nightmare visions beforehand.

35
00:04:52.507 --> 00:04:55.194
- Any clue what's causing it?
- No idea.

36
00:04:56.411 --> 00:04:59.600
The one week I fill in for Jordan,
and it couldn't be some hairy-ass monster?

37
00:04:59.680 --> 00:05:02.637
The same pattern is repeating
around the world,

38
00:05:02.717 --> 00:05:04.671
so there could be an overriding factor.

39
00:05:04.751 --> 00:05:06.775
Perhaps a paranormal element.

40
00:05:06.855 --> 00:05:09.010
Are you talking about magic?

41
00:05:09.690 --> 00:05:11.912
We've come up against
magic before, Batman.

42
00:05:11.992 --> 00:05:16.483
- Xerxes, Trigon, Felix Faust.
- Even Shazam's powers are based in magic.

43
00:05:16.563 --> 00:05:19.035
With as much as you've seen,
can you rule it out?

44
00:05:19.115 --> 00:05:22.674
The criminally insane
don't need magic as an excuse.

45
00:05:22.754 --> 00:05:27.026
I recommend spending more time
on the streets instead of flying over them.

46
00:05:29.742 --> 00:05:32.013
He's even friendlier than they say.

47
00:06:53.828 --> 00:06:58.902
Bollocks! In what bloody plane of
existence does four of a kind lose?

48
00:06:59.733 --> 00:07:03.805
Too, too bad, Constantine.

49
00:07:04.771 --> 00:07:09.142
Have you gained weight?
It looks good on you.

50
00:07:09.442 --> 00:07:12.299
What say you let your soul mate
play a few hands, Jason?

51
00:07:12.379 --> 00:07:15.835
Maybe he'd change my luck.
He'd definitely be less mopey than you.

52
00:07:15.915 --> 00:07:20.773
John Constantine, the man
who perfected the bad idea.

53
00:07:20.853 --> 00:07:23.538
The only reason I came
to this dung heap of a casino

54
00:07:23.618 --> 00:07:26.646
is to find a relic to keep
that monster locked away forever.

55
00:07:26.726 --> 00:07:30.833
Boys, boys! You're boring me.
Let's play, shall we?

56
00:07:48.583 --> 00:07:51.605
My luck's running
as hot as me naughty bits.

57
00:07:52.585 --> 00:07:57.977
But our next group of friends is due
to arrive, so it's time to bust you out.

58
00:07:58.057 --> 00:08:01.447
Copperfield's coming. Presto changeo!

59
00:08:01.527 --> 00:08:04.718
Woman in a box. In a box.

60
00:08:04.798 --> 00:08:08.155
Yeah, he's classy, unlike you.

61
00:08:08.235 --> 00:08:12.942
Are they implying David Copperfield,
television magician, has true power?

62
00:08:13.022 --> 00:08:17.796
Owns a chain of islands and dated
Claudia Schiffer. What do you think?

63
00:08:20.747 --> 00:08:23.335
No cards for me, and...

64
00:08:23.415 --> 00:08:26.507
Looks like you can't call
my bet, Constantine.

65
00:08:26.587 --> 00:08:29.310
By my rules, you lose.

66
00:08:29.390 --> 00:08:31.847
- I raise.
- With what?

67
00:08:31.927 --> 00:08:36.164
- Your ratty soul ain't worth two bits.
- Not two bits.

68
00:08:36.798 --> 00:08:40.879
I'm betting the House,
the House of Mystery.

69
00:08:46.641 --> 00:08:49.469
And since I'm including everything inside,
it looks like you're the one

70
00:08:49.549 --> 00:08:51.946
that can't call, Abnegazar.

71
00:08:52.546 --> 00:08:54.602
Well, what do you say, boys?

72
00:08:54.682 --> 00:08:56.990
I like the action.

73
00:09:11.602 --> 00:09:13.052
I call.

74
00:09:17.605 --> 00:09:20.394
Really? A chipped Dreamstone?

75
00:09:20.474 --> 00:09:22.330
I'm out.

76
00:09:23.010 --> 00:09:26.818
Broken knick-knacks for the House of
Mystery and its contents? Are you mad?

77
00:09:26.898 --> 00:09:30.368
I've got a working soul catcher.

78
00:09:30.449 --> 00:09:33.510
That's Ogid's Eye Spiker?

79
00:09:33.590 --> 00:09:34.935
And the Garazi.

80
00:09:35.015 --> 00:09:40.030
So even if that very magical Dreamstone
doesn't work, it's still a big-ass ruby.

81
00:09:41.060 --> 00:09:45.100
I'd be a poor sport indeed
if I didn't accept your fair wager.

82
00:09:52.639 --> 00:09:56.028
Hell. Now, that's
a losing hand for the ages.

83
00:09:56.108 --> 00:09:59.398
Now, read them and...

84
00:09:59.814 --> 00:10:03.318
- What?
- Do they have an eye doctor in hell?

85
00:10:03.399 --> 00:10:07.534
- I'd make an appointment if I was you.
- You cheated!

86
00:10:10.857 --> 00:10:13.980
Technically, we both cheated.
I just did it better.

87
00:10:14.210 --> 00:10:18.133
- I'll rip your bloody heart out!
- Sorry, mate, I'm using that.

88
00:10:35.400 --> 00:10:38.689
Situation here, Jason.
It's time to call your better half.

89
00:10:38.769 --> 00:10:41.960
Sorry, John, you're on your own.

90
00:10:51.081 --> 00:10:55.488
Oi, I'm gonna roast your nuts
and feed them to you, Constantine.

91
00:11:03.260 --> 00:11:06.282
Gone, gone, the form of man.

92
00:11:06.362 --> 00:11:09.769
Arise the demon, Etrigan!

93
00:11:13.203 --> 00:11:16.827
Once more with words of metered rhyme

94
00:11:16.907 --> 00:11:20.565
comes Etrigan the Slayer just in time.

95
00:11:20.645 --> 00:11:24.168
Easy now, brother.
We're on the same side, right?

96
00:11:24.248 --> 00:11:26.604
Let's use our words.

97
00:11:27.084 --> 00:11:29.973
Are you having a laugh?
We're the Demons Three.

98
00:11:30.053 --> 00:11:32.056
Kill everyone!

99
00:11:41.931 --> 00:11:44.055
You will pay, Constantine.

100
00:11:44.135 --> 00:11:46.591
Your soul will be ours.

101
00:11:46.671 --> 00:11:48.907
Get in line, you prats.

102
00:12:00.416 --> 00:12:02.739
Your ass is grass, Constantine.

103
00:12:02.819 --> 00:12:06.057
And we're the lawnmower.

104
00:12:07.256 --> 00:12:09.913
Since the battle's fought and won,

105
00:12:09.993 --> 00:12:13.532
Jason Blood with me is done.

106
00:12:23.206 --> 00:12:26.063
For 500 years, I've been bound to Etrigan,

107
00:12:26.143 --> 00:12:30.400
fighting to keep him from coming forth,
and you forced me to summon him.

108
00:12:30.480 --> 00:12:32.553
Everything got sorted.

109
00:12:32.633 --> 00:12:36.263
He could have gone on a killing spree.
You don't think.

110
00:12:36.343 --> 00:12:39.260
- You don't consider the cost.
- Yeah, I did.

111
00:12:39.340 --> 00:12:43.461
Weighed it against my being eaten alive
and thought, "Yeah, totally worth it."

112
00:12:45.696 --> 00:12:48.284
You're a world class bastard, John.

113
00:13:15.525 --> 00:13:22.408
And for my finale, I will make this
terrible trio of terrifying Tantors

114
00:13:22.488 --> 00:13:24.902
vanish before your eyes.

115
00:13:50.895 --> 00:13:53.116
I hope those elephants survived.

116
00:13:53.696 --> 00:13:55.920
You don't want PETA on your back.

117
00:13:56.000 --> 00:13:58.504
You're assuming they were real
in the first place.

118
00:14:00.470 --> 00:14:04.594
- How are you, Bruce?
- I'm fine, Zatanna. Busy.

119
00:14:04.674 --> 00:14:07.698
You know where I can find
John Constantine?

120
00:14:07.778 --> 00:14:10.317
- No.
- You must have some idea.

121
00:14:10.397 --> 00:14:12.502
We don't keep in touch.

122
00:14:12.582 --> 00:14:15.185
I know you two have history, so I...

123
00:14:19.255 --> 00:14:21.645
Z, Batman needs to talk with John.

124
00:14:21.725 --> 00:14:23.814
You've got to come along, too.
It's important.

125
00:14:23.894 --> 00:14:26.583
- Is that you, Boston?
- Yeah.

126
00:14:26.663 --> 00:14:30.535
Everything is...
Boy, this guy's mind is tough.

127
00:14:31.299 --> 00:14:33.322
Can't hold...

128
00:14:37.039 --> 00:14:39.129
What is going on?

129
00:14:39.209 --> 00:14:41.813
I'll tell you on the way to John's.

130
00:14:42.996 --> 00:14:45.066
Okay, but I call shotgun.

131
00:14:49.852 --> 00:14:51.742
I don't even think
his kid could fit back here.

132
00:14:51.822 --> 00:14:54.111
Sorry, Boston, but life is for the living.

133
00:14:54.191 --> 00:14:57.112
Boston Brand. He was a circus performer.

134
00:14:57.192 --> 00:15:01.650
Batman's heard of me. Sweet.
Tell him I'm a fan of his, too,

135
00:15:01.730 --> 00:15:04.223
but, you know, be cool about it.

136
00:15:04.303 --> 00:15:08.092
- Yeah, that's him.
- Ask him if he caught one of my shows.

137
00:15:08.172 --> 00:15:13.162
He was a trapeze artist who loved being
famous, especially with the ladies.

138
00:15:13.342 --> 00:15:16.467
- Husbands, not so much.
- You're killing me.

139
00:15:16.547 --> 00:15:19.269
He had a knack for irritating
the wrong people.

140
00:15:19.349 --> 00:15:23.453
<i>Then, about five years ago,
karma caught up with him.</i>

141
00:15:27.089 --> 00:15:30.212
<i>It was a weekend show, full house.</i>

142
00:15:30.292 --> 00:15:34.765
<i>Boston was in the middle
of his death-defying act when...</i>

143
00:16:01.090 --> 00:16:03.981
<i>he died, and that should have been that,</i>

144
00:16:04.061 --> 00:16:07.919
<i>but with Boston,
things tend to get complicated.</i>

145
00:16:08.799 --> 00:16:12.823
<i>His spirit was called
by the goddess Rama Kushna.</i>

146
00:16:14.203 --> 00:16:18.194
<i>She took pity on him and gave him
the power to possess the living,</i>

147
00:16:18.274 --> 00:16:21.030
so he could bring his killer
and others to justice.

148
00:16:21.110 --> 00:16:23.167
Hey, I don't wanna brag, but I'm good.

149
00:16:23.247 --> 00:16:26.408
Why did he feel the need
to write on my walls like a child?

150
00:16:26.488 --> 00:16:28.319
Yeah, he's sorry about that.

151
00:16:30.452 --> 00:16:34.878
Where is this address? GPS doesn't
seem especially useful tonight.

152
00:16:34.958 --> 00:16:39.283
It's not an address. The House
of Mystery tends to move around.

153
00:16:39.363 --> 00:16:43.387
I didn't put the symbols in there
for the GPS to find it.

154
00:16:43.467 --> 00:16:45.290
I wanted the House to come to us.

155
00:17:38.889 --> 00:17:41.393
She can't hold it. Do something.

156
00:17:59.100 --> 00:18:00.045
There.

157
00:18:06.916 --> 00:18:08.953
Into the House!

158
00:18:20.597 --> 00:18:24.420
- Z, you all right?
- Yeah, as soon as you get off me.

159
00:18:24.900 --> 00:18:28.692
I should have known you were the reason
I'm not back in London enjoying a pint.

160
00:18:28.772 --> 00:18:31.561
The House always did like you better.

161
00:18:31.641 --> 00:18:35.265
Odd trio for a road trip.
To what do I owe the visit?

162
00:18:35.395 --> 00:18:39.341
The League thinks that a recent spike
in homicides may have a magical cause.

163
00:18:42.319 --> 00:18:47.209
Told you something stinks. Now we know
someone doesn't want us asking questions.

164
00:18:47.289 --> 00:18:49.679
Looks like you've cracked it
wide open, mate.

165
00:18:49.759 --> 00:18:51.347
What did he say?

166
00:18:51.427 --> 00:18:54.165
I'm not playing telephone between you two.

167
00:18:57.500 --> 00:18:59.338
We online?

168
00:19:00.269 --> 00:19:04.860
Great. Sorry about the Batmobile.
I hope your insurance was paid up.

169
00:19:05.340 --> 00:19:08.077
What, is there even a policy
for something like that?

170
00:19:10.447 --> 00:19:13.771
Hey, I told you not to do that, Orchid.
Use a bloody door.

171
00:19:14.251 --> 00:19:16.587
I am glad to see you are well.

172
00:19:18.788 --> 00:19:22.546
- How new is this one?
- Not what you think.

173
00:19:22.626 --> 00:19:24.547
It's the magic of the House.

174
00:19:24.627 --> 00:19:28.751
Decided it wanted to experience
humanity and gave itself a body.

175
00:19:28.831 --> 00:19:30.869
It sure did.

176
00:19:31.534 --> 00:19:36.593
A spirit whose existence
is not its own, like myself.

177
00:19:37.273 --> 00:19:39.110
Interesting.

178
00:19:40.741 --> 00:19:44.133
Yeah, we are that.

179
00:19:44.213 --> 00:19:46.837
Dead smooth you are, mate.

180
00:19:47.117 --> 00:19:49.922
Hey, it's been a while, you know?

181
00:19:52.188 --> 00:19:56.952
Powerful in true magic. Angry at John.

182
00:19:57.294 --> 00:19:59.716
This, I understand.

183
00:20:00.296 --> 00:20:04.255
Yet you still have feelings for him.

184
00:20:05.118 --> 00:20:06.989
I could kill him.

185
00:20:14.243 --> 00:20:16.632
You exude pain.

186
00:20:16.712 --> 00:20:21.271
Your life is a patchwork of blackness
with no time for joy.

187
00:20:21.851 --> 00:20:24.123
How do you cope with it?

188
00:20:25.755 --> 00:20:28.026
I have a butler.

189
00:20:30.959 --> 00:20:32.997
That was enlightening.

190
00:20:36.332 --> 00:20:39.404
Well, I guess we should have
that chinwag about now.

191
00:20:42.137 --> 00:20:44.875
- <i>Demons!</i>
- <i>It's not me!</i>

192
00:20:46.243 --> 00:20:49.431
<i>I've given birth to the devil. It's the...</i>

193
00:20:49.911 --> 00:20:52.920
Rama Kushna says this will break down
the walls between the planes.

194
00:20:53.000 --> 00:20:55.005
Even the afterlife will be affected.

195
00:20:55.085 --> 00:20:58.340
Yeah, it's dodgy, all right.
I'll look into it.

196
00:20:58.420 --> 00:21:01.444
Meanwhile, the House
will drop you wherever you'd like.

197
00:21:02.024 --> 00:21:05.715
Rama says we have to work together.
Come on! It's a dream team.

198
00:21:05.795 --> 00:21:09.085
You, me, Zatanna, Batman,
maybe even the Justice League.

199
00:21:09.165 --> 00:21:13.455
The capes and tights crew,
useless against dark magic.

200
00:21:13.535 --> 00:21:16.859
That's why we need you. You can lead us.

201
00:21:16.939 --> 00:21:21.564
Boston, do I strike you as a team player?
Much less a team leader.

202
00:21:21.644 --> 00:21:24.801
Point is, even deities can get it wrong.

203
00:21:24.881 --> 00:21:28.370
It's how we got the appendix,
Neanderthals and reality TV.

204
00:21:28.450 --> 00:21:30.574
Z, your help I could use.

205
00:21:30.654 --> 00:21:33.543
Okay, if we do it as a group.

206
00:21:35.023 --> 00:21:39.281
This is the monkey cage
in Sumatra all over again.

207
00:21:39.361 --> 00:21:41.501
"We need to save the monkeys," she said.

208
00:21:41.581 --> 00:21:45.389
- You're such an ass.
- Not the monkeys.

209
00:21:45.469 --> 00:21:49.993
Says the man who has Newcastle
and 100 other screw-ups on his resume,

210
00:21:50.073 --> 00:21:53.545
- costing lives and souls.
- But not monkeys.

211
00:21:53.625 --> 00:21:56.266
- You're still way ahead on dead monkeys.
- They used to be a thing.

212
00:21:56.346 --> 00:21:59.350
- You just have to make things...
- We're wasting time.

213
00:22:00.482 --> 00:22:04.248
He's dead, and I accept the risks,
so can we get to it,

214
00:22:04.328 --> 00:22:06.958
or do you two need a timeout?

215
00:22:09.459 --> 00:22:12.998
Fine and dandy. Let's take a walk
on the dark side then.

216
00:22:16.833 --> 00:22:18.870
Coming, team?

217
00:22:24.306 --> 00:22:28.198
Stop being a child and slow down.
Where are we going?

218
00:22:28.278 --> 00:22:31.250
- Ritchie's.
- Have you talked to him lately?

219
00:22:31.330 --> 00:22:34.203
I know he's pissed.
You don't have to remind me, love.

220
00:22:34.283 --> 00:22:39.123
- It's on my CV, remember?
- No, really, has he told you...

221
00:22:40.691 --> 00:22:43.831
No. He's dying.

222
00:22:43.911 --> 00:22:46.549
John Constantine,

223
00:22:46.629 --> 00:22:52.288
purveyor of the dark arts
and lifeline of last resort.

224
00:22:52.768 --> 00:22:58.660
No matter. Your friend's soul
will be collected,

225
00:22:58.740 --> 00:23:02.848
and there's nothing
you can do to alter that.

226
00:23:02.928 --> 00:23:06.835
Why don't you go do something
useful, like haunt a house?

227
00:23:06.915 --> 00:23:11.823
- Who's he talking to now?
- Shrouds. They deliver souls to hell.

228
00:23:13.890 --> 00:23:15.946
They're drawn to you.

229
00:23:16.426 --> 00:23:18.916
Maybe it's your cologne, Batsy.

230
00:23:19.596 --> 00:23:23.126
This one has cheated us many times.

231
00:23:23.366 --> 00:23:25.887
It is vexing.

232
00:23:31.207 --> 00:23:34.596
This has been lovely,
but it's time for you lot to bugger off.

233
00:23:34.976 --> 00:23:41.371
When the time comes, I'll be the one
to collect your soul, Constantine.

234
00:23:41.451 --> 00:23:43.488
Yeah, yeah.

235
00:23:45.788 --> 00:23:49.313
I thought I felt
a disturbance in the force.

236
00:23:50.692 --> 00:23:53.030
How you doing, Johnny boy?

237
00:23:53.530 --> 00:23:57.889
Zatanna and Batman?

238
00:23:58.968 --> 00:24:01.123
What the hell?

239
00:24:01.503 --> 00:24:03.927
Tell you everything inside, mate.

240
00:24:11.947 --> 00:24:13.803
You poor thing.

241
00:24:13.883 --> 00:24:17.139
Yeah, I may have lied
the last time we talked,

242
00:24:17.219 --> 00:24:21.042
about exactly how fast
I'm sledding downhill.

243
00:24:21.122 --> 00:24:23.227
I'm sorry about that.

244
00:24:24.294 --> 00:24:26.516
But it means a lot you're here, John.

245
00:24:26.596 --> 00:24:31.121
And, hey, you don't have
to say it. You're forgiven.

246
00:24:31.801 --> 00:24:34.524
Still wondering what Batman's
doing in my living room.

247
00:24:34.604 --> 00:24:37.941
And when is he gonna shut up, right?

248
00:24:38.974 --> 00:24:41.779
What? What's with the face?

249
00:24:43.045 --> 00:24:45.600
You're not here to say
you're sorry, are you?

250
00:24:45.680 --> 00:24:50.723
Of course I am, but I was looking
to borrow the Keshanti Key as well.

251
00:24:50.803 --> 00:24:53.543
Unbelievable.

252
00:24:53.623 --> 00:24:57.413
- I tried to tell him on the way.
- Yeah, it's not your fault, Z.

253
00:24:57.493 --> 00:25:00.917
Just like everything,
this is rock star Johnny's fault.

254
00:25:00.997 --> 00:25:04.721
I was with you when it happened,
Ritchie. We were side by side.

255
00:25:04.801 --> 00:25:06.989
Yeah, yeah, yeah, side by side.

256
00:25:07.069 --> 00:25:10.566
But I got the weird
magical cancer while you,

257
00:25:10.646 --> 00:25:12.722
you added to your rep. Isn't that right?

258
00:25:12.802 --> 00:25:16.199
Look, me not making proper amends
isn't related to the Key,

259
00:25:16.279 --> 00:25:19.286
which, truth be told,
you're not gonna need, mate.

260
00:25:19.366 --> 00:25:21.085
John!

261
00:25:26.655 --> 00:25:28.460
Getting that a lot lately.

262
00:25:28.540 --> 00:25:31.814
You can go screw yourself.
I am not giving you crap.

263
00:25:31.894 --> 00:25:34.751
Your anger is understandable,
but you need to reconsider.

264
00:25:34.831 --> 00:25:37.269
Innocent lives are at stake.

265
00:25:48.577 --> 00:25:51.933
Well, doctors say
an upbeat attitude can help,

266
00:25:52.013 --> 00:25:56.740
so what I'll focus on today
is that I met Batman.

267
00:25:56.820 --> 00:26:01.477
Force of good.
It was also nice seeing you, Zatanna.

268
00:26:01.957 --> 00:26:04.361
Now, if you'll excuse me...

269
00:26:07.897 --> 00:26:10.234
You can show yourselves out.

270
00:26:34.357 --> 00:26:35.694
This him?

271
00:26:37.493 --> 00:26:41.333
Father of the year.
I'll need the gear now.

272
00:26:43.865 --> 00:26:47.089
- How does this work?
- It's basically a magical shortcut.

273
00:26:47.169 --> 00:26:49.126
It lets me access
different planes of existence

274
00:26:49.206 --> 00:26:51.593
without doing 20-odd hours
of incantations.

275
00:26:51.673 --> 00:26:52.866
In this case,

276
00:26:52.946 --> 00:26:56.917
I'll poke around this poor sod's memories
to see how his madness began.

277
00:26:58.982 --> 00:27:01.734
And, more importantly, what caused it.

278
00:27:03.886 --> 00:27:07.125
What are you doing here?
I'm calling security.

279
00:27:09.525 --> 00:27:12.731
I'll make sure the looky-loos
stay out of our hair.

280
00:27:14.196 --> 00:27:17.903
Z, give me a psychic shout
if this body comes under attack.

281
00:27:17.983 --> 00:27:19.656
Wouldn't do to be trapped inside, now.

282
00:27:19.736 --> 00:27:23.175
Wouldn't do to go in alone,
and since I'm right here...

283
00:27:23.255 --> 00:27:26.445
Too dangerous.
You're out of practice, love.

284
00:27:26.525 --> 00:27:29.265
Look, you wanted me along. I'm here.

285
00:27:29.345 --> 00:27:32.783
I'm not waiting in the wings.
Let's do this.

286
00:27:59.108 --> 00:28:01.297
Z? You okay?

287
00:28:01.377 --> 00:28:03.035
I'm fine.

288
00:28:08.984 --> 00:28:11.774
I've never liked this sort of magic.

289
00:28:11.854 --> 00:28:14.577
I can feel darkness seeping inside me.

290
00:28:14.957 --> 00:28:17.329
How you stand it is beyond me.

291
00:28:17.409 --> 00:28:21.250
It's all about control.
If you ever need a refresher...

292
00:28:21.330 --> 00:28:24.970
We've had this conversation.
I haven't changed my mind.

293
00:28:27.970 --> 00:28:30.927
Sure, sit out the war
between good and evil.

294
00:28:31.007 --> 00:28:34.464
After all, you've got a good thing going
being applauded by mindless twits.

295
00:28:34.544 --> 00:28:36.632
Really? Now?

296
00:28:36.712 --> 00:28:38.384
Good a time as ever, I reckon.

297
00:28:38.464 --> 00:28:41.654
- I'll teach you to talk back.
- No!

298
00:28:42.284 --> 00:28:45.741
The magic I perform
brings people happiness.

299
00:28:45.821 --> 00:28:48.011
You sure it's not
the two drink minimum, love?

300
00:28:48.091 --> 00:28:49.779
You're such a pessimist.

301
00:28:49.859 --> 00:28:52.343
Wrong. I expect the worst,

302
00:28:52.423 --> 00:28:56.284
so I prepare for the worst,
and when the worst happens, I'm ready.

303
00:28:56.364 --> 00:28:59.521
But my outlook doesn't alter
the reality of the world.

304
00:28:59.601 --> 00:29:02.591
- <i>Steven, stop!</i>
- <i>Leave me alone!</i>

305
00:29:02.871 --> 00:29:05.194
Another precious moment.

306
00:29:05.274 --> 00:29:07.429
There was joy, too.

307
00:29:07.509 --> 00:29:09.813
His madness swept it away.

308
00:29:49.384 --> 00:29:51.388
Who dropped the bed pan?

309
00:30:25.421 --> 00:30:28.144
This is it.
This was the morning of his madness.

310
00:30:28.224 --> 00:30:31.613
- What do you think will set him off?
- My guess is the Sudoku.

311
00:30:31.693 --> 00:30:34.083
He's got two 9s in the same row.

312
00:30:34.163 --> 00:30:35.832
John.

313
00:30:45.373 --> 00:30:48.363
Run! Run! Run!

314
00:30:48.843 --> 00:30:51.748
Run! Let's get out of here!

315
00:30:56.218 --> 00:30:59.456
Come on, fellow. Eat a piece of fruit?

316
00:32:08.892 --> 00:32:10.727
Here it is.

317
00:32:18.067 --> 00:32:20.071
We've got to get out of here.

318
00:32:21.736 --> 00:32:23.593
One more second.

319
00:32:25.842 --> 00:32:27.779
Now, John. There's no time.

320
00:32:34.517 --> 00:32:36.387
Got it.

321
00:33:00.808 --> 00:33:04.433
- Shit's really hit the fan.
- You had to go there, Boston.

322
00:33:05.013 --> 00:33:07.017
Let's get the hell out of here.

323
00:33:17.159 --> 00:33:19.881
- I don't recognize it.
- Me, neither.

324
00:33:19.961 --> 00:33:22.651
But if there's a person alive
who can, it's Ritchie.

325
00:33:22.731 --> 00:33:25.653
Are you forgetting when you made
your friend despise you?

326
00:33:25.733 --> 00:33:28.272
This is too bloody important
for hurt feelings.

327
00:33:34.777 --> 00:33:37.533
- Constantine.
- Bollocks.

328
00:33:37.913 --> 00:33:40.617
You've arrived in time to witness my...

329
00:33:42.217 --> 00:33:44.054
Ritchie!

330
00:33:47.790 --> 00:33:49.545
Get back, you bastards!

331
00:33:49.625 --> 00:33:51.895
John, help Ritchie.

332
00:33:54.295 --> 00:33:55.900
Take that! Boom!

333
00:33:56.098 --> 00:34:00.003
- No pulse.
- We know! We know! Come on!

334
00:34:15.417 --> 00:34:16.540
Why?

335
00:34:21.823 --> 00:34:24.212
I see you have a few tricks of your own?

336
00:34:24.292 --> 00:34:26.563
Not everything requires magic.

337
00:34:42.644 --> 00:34:45.133
Make sure he sees that
right when he wakes up.

338
00:34:45.213 --> 00:34:46.983
If he wakes.

339
00:34:49.719 --> 00:34:53.876
We need to talk, you and I,
but if you try and summon Etrigan,

340
00:34:53.956 --> 00:34:57.681
I'll fill your lungs with bile
before the first verse is done.

341
00:34:57.761 --> 00:34:58.967
Savvy?

342
00:35:06.635 --> 00:35:09.023
The situation was not how it seemed.

343
00:35:09.103 --> 00:35:13.077
The apartment was like that
when I arrived. Richard as well.

344
00:35:13.157 --> 00:35:16.665
- Come on! You were all over him.
- I was attempting to help.

345
00:35:16.745 --> 00:35:20.151
When you burst in,
I knew I'd get blamed, so I ran.

346
00:35:20.231 --> 00:35:23.739
- Do you believe him?
- Jason's not the murdery type.

347
00:35:23.819 --> 00:35:27.577
He's chock full of honor, loyalty,
and rubbish of that sort.

348
00:35:27.657 --> 00:35:30.060
Then tell us why you were there.

349
00:35:31.109 --> 00:35:34.833
Richard is known as a collector
of the arcane and supernatural.

350
00:35:34.913 --> 00:35:39.205
I wanted to see if he had something
that could gain me access to this place.

351
00:35:39.435 --> 00:35:41.739
Why would you wanna break in here?

352
00:35:42.939 --> 00:35:44.394
For this.

353
00:35:44.474 --> 00:35:48.914
The single most powerful conduit
of evil in the history of the world.

354
00:35:48.994 --> 00:35:51.651
He named it the Dreamstone.

355
00:35:52.081 --> 00:35:55.018
But it's really the stuff of nightmares.

356
00:35:57.720 --> 00:36:00.342
<i>I was a young knight, green as grass.</i>

357
00:36:00.422 --> 00:36:04.379
<i>With visions of battle-won glory
dancing in my head.</i>

358
00:36:04.459 --> 00:36:08.900
<i>Needless to say,
these were dispelled thoroughly.</i>

359
00:36:10.165 --> 00:36:12.418
<i>He called himself Destiny,</i>

360
00:36:12.918 --> 00:36:16.359
<i>but Merlin told us he
was a man of science one time,</i>

361
00:36:16.439 --> 00:36:18.474
<i>before he went insane.</i>

362
00:36:18.674 --> 00:36:22.764
<i>Destiny forged the Dreamstone
with black magic and his soul.</i>

363
00:36:22.844 --> 00:36:26.535
<i>He used it to subject people
to their most terrifying nightmares</i>

364
00:36:26.615 --> 00:36:29.087
<i>and then feed off their torment.</i>

365
00:37:40.688 --> 00:37:44.195
<i>It was actually the demon Etrigan
who won the day.</i>

366
00:37:46.629 --> 00:37:51.786
To battle, Etrigan. Should you succeed,
I will release you of your bond to me.

367
00:37:52.216 --> 00:37:54.739
If freedom is what's up for trade,

368
00:37:54.819 --> 00:37:58.091
then Destiny's as good as slayed.

369
00:38:32.073 --> 00:38:35.548
You haven't won, Merlin. This isn't over.

370
00:38:35.628 --> 00:38:37.831
I swear it.

371
00:38:49.291 --> 00:38:51.914
Release me, Merlin, from your care.

372
00:38:51.994 --> 00:38:55.668
My duty's done. 'Tis only fair.

373
00:38:55.748 --> 00:38:59.885
I'm afraid that's not possible,
friend Demon.

374
00:39:05.740 --> 00:39:09.298
I apologize to both you and Jason Blood,

375
00:39:09.378 --> 00:39:13.851
but your future portends a shared destiny.

376
00:39:16.351 --> 00:39:21.277
Caught now, imprisoned in the form of man.

377
00:39:21.889 --> 00:39:25.828
I fix the demon, Etrigan.

378
00:39:37.339 --> 00:39:42.008
<i>It was also the beginning
of my eternal life sentence with Etrigan.</i>

379
00:39:46.948 --> 00:39:48.904
I didn't think you'd give it up willingly,

380
00:39:48.984 --> 00:39:54.058
and though this piece is useless without
the other half, it's far from powerless.

381
00:39:54.539 --> 00:39:55.828
Safe enough where it is.

382
00:39:55.908 --> 00:39:59.979
Displayed like a tourist trinket
in a Karachi bazaar?

383
00:40:01.396 --> 00:40:02.696
Neat, isn't it?

384
00:40:02.776 --> 00:40:06.713
The House keeps my valuables out of phase,
so they don't go wondering off.

385
00:40:06.793 --> 00:40:09.405
But, still, the timing
of the Stone's appearance and its power

386
00:40:09.485 --> 00:40:12.160
indicates that it's somehow
involved with these crimes.

387
00:40:12.240 --> 00:40:16.017
Which is why it stays here,
where only I can get to it.

388
00:40:16.227 --> 00:40:18.406
I think me, them,
and everyone else who knows you

389
00:40:18.486 --> 00:40:20.617
might want it to be somewhere else.

390
00:40:21.782 --> 00:40:24.587
Your friend is awake.

391
00:40:26.621 --> 00:40:29.927
Ritchie, who was it? Who did this to you?

392
00:40:30.242 --> 00:40:32.051
Faust.

393
00:40:32.361 --> 00:40:35.466
Felix Faust. You sure?

394
00:40:49.177 --> 00:40:50.882
There you are, you old bastard.

395
00:40:50.962 --> 00:40:55.837
I give you wizard and asshole
extraordinaire, Felix Faust.

396
00:40:55.917 --> 00:41:00.190
Hell, I should have put it together.
Conjuring a whirlwind is just his style.

397
00:41:02.356 --> 00:41:05.848
The League had a run-in with Faust,
but his location isn't in our database.

398
00:41:06.128 --> 00:41:10.619
Yeah, wizards don't make a habit of
signing up for credit cards or social media.

399
00:41:10.699 --> 00:41:12.965
His grandly named Observatory
of the Cosmos

400
00:41:13.045 --> 00:41:16.607
is hidden from the likes of you
and Superman, but not from me.

401
00:41:20.308 --> 00:41:22.345
Felix Faust.

402
00:41:32.920 --> 00:41:35.046
- What's happening?
- If this were a computer,

403
00:41:35.126 --> 00:41:36.760
I'd say it's frozen.

404
00:41:37.459 --> 00:41:38.846
Cheers.

405
00:41:38.926 --> 00:41:43.251
Felix Faust would take precautions
against locator spells.

406
00:41:43.331 --> 00:41:44.887
There's another way,

407
00:41:44.967 --> 00:41:49.425
but it involves asking a favor of someone
that I don't have the best relationship with.

408
00:41:49.505 --> 00:41:52.527
Someone else dislikes you? Shocking.

409
00:41:52.807 --> 00:41:55.297
Your friend slips from the mortal plane.

410
00:41:55.377 --> 00:41:58.934
- John...
- Keep him alive and safe. Understand?

411
00:41:59.014 --> 00:42:00.869
That is not my purpose.

412
00:42:00.949 --> 00:42:04.172
I don't give a flying shag
what you think your bloody purpose is.

413
00:42:04.252 --> 00:42:07.157
I order you to help him
any and every way you're able.

414
00:42:10.893 --> 00:42:12.663
Let's go.

415
00:42:15.764 --> 00:42:17.853
All right, I'll ask.

416
00:42:17.933 --> 00:42:21.222
Why are we in the middle
of a godforsaken swamp?

417
00:42:21.302 --> 00:42:24.993
It's a favorite hidey hole
of one Alec Holland,

418
00:42:25.073 --> 00:42:28.829
whose corpse was taken to be
the most recent Avatar of the Green.

419
00:42:28.909 --> 00:42:30.999
Bet you won't find that
on your bloody cell phone.

420
00:42:31.079 --> 00:42:34.380
Our data's more factual.
Alec Holland was murdered by terrorists.

421
00:42:34.460 --> 00:42:37.339
His body was never recovered.
End of story.

422
00:42:37.419 --> 00:42:39.223
Not quite.

423
00:42:42.824 --> 00:42:46.497
Go away!

424
00:42:57.239 --> 00:42:59.361
Swamp Thing!

425
00:42:59.441 --> 00:43:03.848
I know you're seeing this.
Get out here, or the posies get it!

426
00:43:16.424 --> 00:43:19.296
John Constantine.

427
00:43:20.429 --> 00:43:23.867
You dare threaten the green.

428
00:43:29.770 --> 00:43:32.394
Dude, your social skills are horrendous.

429
00:43:33.174 --> 00:43:37.416
Please, we aren't here to harm
any plants, but our need is urgent.

430
00:43:37.496 --> 00:43:40.887
Don't let your feelings for John
stop you from doing what's right.

431
00:43:44.786 --> 00:43:47.708
You have a garden.

432
00:43:47.788 --> 00:43:51.172
Yes, I find it relaxing,

433
00:43:51.252 --> 00:43:53.647
and I water it every week.

434
00:43:53.895 --> 00:43:58.452
We need to find a man,
a wizard named Felix Faust.

435
00:43:58.532 --> 00:44:03.123
A single human among your teeming masses.

436
00:44:03.203 --> 00:44:08.111
I only know John Constantine
because he enrages me.

437
00:44:12.214 --> 00:44:14.970
Faust lives in an observatory
which is invisible.

438
00:44:15.050 --> 00:44:18.874
It's a place where dark magic
would infect the earth below it.

439
00:44:19.454 --> 00:44:24.461
I will take you there
so you are no longer here.

440
00:44:38.406 --> 00:44:42.212
The place you seek is there.

441
00:44:54.790 --> 00:44:57.193
That place is heavily warded.

442
00:45:01.212 --> 00:45:04.902
I know we've had our differences,
but we could really use your help.

443
00:45:04.982 --> 00:45:09.123
If we don't get a handle on this rotter,
he'll threaten all of humanity.

444
00:45:10.105 --> 00:45:12.061
What of it?

445
00:45:12.641 --> 00:45:15.880
You were once human, just like me.

446
00:45:17.679 --> 00:45:19.467
No longer.

447
00:45:19.547 --> 00:45:22.836
Perhaps his actions are a kind of justice,

448
00:45:23.316 --> 00:45:28.358
for who destroys more
of the green than your kind?

449
00:45:33.828 --> 00:45:36.419
And Swamp Thing has left the building.

450
00:45:36.499 --> 00:45:39.735
- Guess we do it the hard way.
- Or not.

451
00:45:39.815 --> 00:45:43.265
Gone, gone, the form of man.

452
00:45:43.405 --> 00:45:47.444
Arise the demon Etrigan!

453
00:46:09.932 --> 00:46:11.702
What...

454
00:46:14.468 --> 00:46:19.260
- Who dares?
- I, Etrigan, bring down this house

455
00:46:19.340 --> 00:46:22.279
and build a tomb for Felix Faust!

456
00:46:27.882 --> 00:46:30.371
As if I would stoop
to brawling with a demon.

457
00:46:30.451 --> 00:46:32.889
Fight others of your filthy kind.

458
00:46:43.931 --> 00:46:48.354
From hell though we may be,
it does not make us family!

459
00:47:08.890 --> 00:47:11.313
Do you like what I've done with the place?

460
00:47:11.393 --> 00:47:14.431
No woman can speak
in my sanctum sanctorum.

461
00:47:14.511 --> 00:47:19.017
I conjured it just for you
and, of course, men everywhere.

462
00:47:32.246 --> 00:47:36.659
As a fellow showman, this is no way
to treat your guests. Now, settle down!

463
00:47:44.592 --> 00:47:47.949
Stop hitting yourself. Stop hitting
yourself. Stop hitting yourself.

464
00:47:49.229 --> 00:47:52.434
Not everything can be solved
with your peashooter.

465
00:47:56.171 --> 00:48:01.679
Just because you're dead doesn't
mean you're beyond my retribution.

466
00:48:14.322 --> 00:48:15.798
Is that it?

467
00:48:15.878 --> 00:48:20.763
Well, it's off to the old magicians home
for you, mate. Pudding night is Thursday.

468
00:48:30.772 --> 00:48:35.563
Try that fireball once more, Constantine.
I'd love to see you cook your own goose.

469
00:48:35.643 --> 00:48:37.466
Let me...

470
00:48:57.498 --> 00:48:59.599
I take it back. That thing is useful.

471
00:49:41.074 --> 00:49:43.364
Zatanna, where are you, darling?

472
00:49:43.444 --> 00:49:46.234
I know you can't speak,
but give me a wave.

473
00:49:46.314 --> 00:49:49.119
You're the only one here
that's really a threat.

474
00:49:56.090 --> 00:49:59.996
There you are. This will sting a bit.

475
00:50:22.482 --> 00:50:28.290
Stored magic? Really?
It's the TV dinner of spell casting, dear.

476
00:50:30.891 --> 00:50:33.796
Here's what real magic looks like.

477
00:51:09.329 --> 00:51:10.766
Z!

478
00:51:48.068 --> 00:51:50.639
Z, are you daft? Stop!

479
00:51:52.507 --> 00:51:54.728
I will kill you, woman!

480
00:52:25.940 --> 00:52:27.464
Z, don't!

481
00:52:30.644 --> 00:52:34.102
Don't kill him. You can't.

482
00:52:34.182 --> 00:52:35.686
Out of my way, John.

483
00:52:35.766 --> 00:52:39.537
If no blood is spilled,
your soul is in the clear.

484
00:52:48.629 --> 00:52:51.685
Get control, Z, just like I taught you.

485
00:52:51.765 --> 00:52:55.672
Easy-peasy, lemon squeezy. Deep breaths.

486
00:52:56.503 --> 00:52:58.341
Let it go, love.

487
00:53:19.793 --> 00:53:22.451
Do you see why I can't do what you do?

488
00:53:22.931 --> 00:53:27.221
You lost control is all.
Happens to the best of us.

489
00:53:27.301 --> 00:53:29.605
You've seen me in action, right?

490
00:53:31.070 --> 00:53:34.077
Yeah, once or twice.

491
00:53:35.210 --> 00:53:41.383
Why are you here? I haven't done anything
to warrant this kind of response.

492
00:53:43.017 --> 00:53:45.005
This yours?

493
00:53:45.085 --> 00:53:46.627
I don't know. Maybe.

494
00:53:46.707 --> 00:53:50.378
I have several hundred rings
of varying design and properties.

495
00:53:50.808 --> 00:53:52.447
It isn't him.

496
00:53:52.527 --> 00:53:55.917
Felix Faust isn't the one
behind the nightmare crimes.

497
00:53:55.997 --> 00:53:59.954
He summoned our old poker buddies
in their more massive forms.

498
00:54:00.034 --> 00:54:01.555
The hell does it all mean?

499
00:54:01.635 --> 00:54:05.309
It means Felix Faust had access
to the artifact whenever he wanted.

500
00:54:05.589 --> 00:54:07.746
What artifact?

501
00:54:07.926 --> 00:54:09.882
Well, we're back to square one, then.

502
00:54:09.962 --> 00:54:14.069
Unfortunately, no. We were sent here
by your friend, remember?

503
00:54:14.149 --> 00:54:17.821
- But Ritchie's dying.
- Is he?

504
00:54:41.542 --> 00:54:45.882
Boy, boy. I think I got closer
to death than I planned.

505
00:54:48.479 --> 00:54:49.997
Bad girl.

506
00:54:50.077 --> 00:54:54.542
See, now, you were told to do everything
to help me by the master of the House,

507
00:54:54.622 --> 00:54:57.594
and that does not include punching.

508
00:54:59.293 --> 00:55:01.698
Bring me to the main room.

509
00:55:06.533 --> 00:55:09.238
I'll take it from here, beautiful.

510
00:55:11.306 --> 00:55:13.394
But I need you out of my hair for now,

511
00:55:13.474 --> 00:55:17.413
so why don't you just go
for a little walk?

512
00:55:46.741 --> 00:55:50.042
Yeah! That's the stuff.

513
00:55:59.052 --> 00:56:00.408
Why aren't we inside?

514
00:56:00.488 --> 00:56:04.112
Because Ritchie's bloody well
taken control of the House.

515
00:56:04.192 --> 00:56:08.598
This is what you get for having mates.
Boston, can you get inside?

516
00:56:14.201 --> 00:56:16.090
That would be a no.

517
00:56:16.970 --> 00:56:20.909
Ritchie, you're gonna listen to me
whether you like it or not.

518
00:56:23.109 --> 00:56:25.080
Open the door.

519
00:56:25.913 --> 00:56:28.017
Do you hear? Open it!

520
00:56:36.022 --> 00:56:38.226
Too late, Johnny Boy.

521
00:56:52.874 --> 00:56:54.296
Ritchie, please!

522
00:56:54.576 --> 00:56:57.215
Stop while there's still time
to save your soul.

523
00:56:57.295 --> 00:57:01.001
Says the man who skates
away from everything.

524
00:57:01.081 --> 00:57:02.536
Since you got me infected,

525
00:57:02.616 --> 00:57:07.541
I've looked all around the world
for a cure and I've finally found it.

526
00:57:07.721 --> 00:57:11.478
A small piece of the Dreamstone.
It's sentient.

527
00:57:11.558 --> 00:57:15.917
It told me how to get the Demons Three
to bring the rest of it to Earth.

528
00:57:16.597 --> 00:57:20.120
It would've been so easy
to take it from them.

529
00:57:20.200 --> 00:57:24.525
Of course, rock star Johnny
screwed everything sideways.

530
00:57:25.005 --> 00:57:29.863
So we had to frame Faust
and get you to bring me here.

531
00:57:29.943 --> 00:57:33.901
Now I'm immortal and supercharged!

532
00:57:33.981 --> 00:57:37.805
You've been played for a sap.
The Stone isn't sentient.

533
00:57:37.885 --> 00:57:41.476
What's left of Destiny's soul was
whispering sweet nothings in your ear,

534
00:57:41.556 --> 00:57:45.880
getting you to commit atrocities
to gain power and make his move.

535
00:57:45.960 --> 00:57:48.149
You're just pissed 'cause I won.

536
00:57:48.429 --> 00:57:50.600
I wish that were the case.

537
00:57:51.732 --> 00:57:53.735
This can't be right.

538
00:57:56.002 --> 00:57:57.638
No!

539
00:58:00.940 --> 00:58:03.613
Wait! Wait! We... we had a deal!

540
00:58:05.647 --> 00:58:07.650
We had a deal!

541
00:58:18.792 --> 00:58:21.596
Five hundred years, I've waited.

542
00:58:23.197 --> 00:58:25.568
Five hundred years, I've planned.

543
00:58:27.634 --> 00:58:30.924
Really? I guess 500 must be the new 300.

544
00:58:31.004 --> 00:58:33.695
What say we share
your beauty secrets over a pint?

545
00:58:33.775 --> 00:58:37.112
A god does not prattle with mortals.

546
00:58:56.397 --> 00:59:00.088
- She gonna be okay?
- I... I don't know.

547
00:59:00.668 --> 00:59:03.190
The amount of magic she's used,

548
00:59:03.270 --> 00:59:05.674
sometimes you don't recover.

549
00:59:10.677 --> 00:59:12.866
I should have never led her back.

550
00:59:12.946 --> 00:59:14.601
Selfish bastard, I am.

551
00:59:14.681 --> 00:59:18.284
You've done what you can for now,
but we have to stop Destiny,

552
00:59:18.364 --> 00:59:20.474
or everyone's at risk.

553
00:59:20.554 --> 00:59:25.478
He's right. He'll have this city by midnight,
the Eastern Seaboard by dawn.

554
00:59:25.558 --> 00:59:29.016
Then, what's to stop him? He'll be a god.

555
00:59:29.096 --> 00:59:31.804
We don't need another one
of those mucking about.

556
00:59:32.199 --> 00:59:34.069
All right.

557
01:00:13.441 --> 01:00:15.062
Get 'em!

558
01:00:15.342 --> 01:00:18.231
They're everywhere! Everywhere!

559
01:00:18.311 --> 01:00:20.134
Yes.

560
01:00:20.614 --> 01:00:22.503
Yes.

561
01:00:22.583 --> 01:00:24.384
<i>My will be done.</i>

562
01:00:29.857 --> 01:00:33.413
Fool! How can you hope to defeat a god?

563
01:00:33.493 --> 01:00:37.351
Not only can I sense you,
you cannot defeat my shield.

564
01:00:37.431 --> 01:00:40.470
Since when does God need a force shield?

565
01:00:51.846 --> 01:00:53.867
The Justice League are on their way.

566
01:00:53.947 --> 01:00:55.902
Suppose that couldn't be helped,

567
01:00:55.982 --> 01:00:59.940
but make sure they stay well away
from Destiny, to not be struck mad,

568
01:01:00.020 --> 01:01:03.892
unless you want a bunch of crazed
super blokes ripping apart the city.

569
01:01:07.126 --> 01:01:09.731
A little late for that, my friend.

570
01:01:25.378 --> 01:01:28.616
<i>John, listen to me.
You've been affected by magic.</i>

571
01:01:31.052 --> 01:01:33.522
<i>Get away to space now.</i>

572
01:01:46.333 --> 01:01:48.255
Sorry to have to ask this, Jason.

573
01:01:48.335 --> 01:01:50.842
At least you're asking.

574
01:01:50.922 --> 01:01:53.744
Gone, gone, the form of man.

575
01:01:53.824 --> 01:01:57.348
Rise the demon Etrigan!

576
01:01:57.978 --> 01:02:01.468
So Constantine calls once more.

577
01:02:01.548 --> 01:02:04.005
Just like a greedy, wanton...

578
01:02:04.085 --> 01:02:06.074
Save the bloody rhymes, and top that git!

579
01:02:06.154 --> 01:02:08.224
Killjoy.

580
01:02:12.993 --> 01:02:16.318
I've had many years
to think about you, Etrigan.

581
01:02:27.340 --> 01:02:30.041
Call this poetic justice.

582
01:02:44.624 --> 01:02:46.628
Holy crap.

583
01:02:51.898 --> 01:02:54.654
Looks like you've finally
beat the curse, my boy.

584
01:02:54.734 --> 01:02:57.072
Wish it were under happier circumstances.

585
01:02:58.905 --> 01:03:01.395
- What are you doing?
- Calling for help.

586
01:03:01.475 --> 01:03:04.945
I just hope he doesn't realize
it's me doing the calling.

587
01:03:20.527 --> 01:03:22.917
Who dares strike at me?

588
01:03:23.247 --> 01:03:27.388
The Defender of the Green...

589
01:03:27.468 --> 01:03:30.460
Swamp Thing.

590
01:03:49.923 --> 01:03:51.593
Perfect.

591
01:04:02.802 --> 01:04:05.520
Glad to see you
back on your feet, Zatanna.

592
01:04:12.813 --> 01:04:15.517
Whatever you're gonna do, do it fast.

593
01:05:03.463 --> 01:05:08.137
The so-called Guardian of the Green
who secretly hopes to be human again.

594
01:05:08.869 --> 01:05:11.639
Let me dispel you of that notion.

595
01:05:28.020 --> 01:05:30.225
Back to the dirt...

596
01:05:31.257 --> 01:05:33.462
where you belong.

597
01:05:44.837 --> 01:05:48.061
He's getting more powerful by the second.
What the hell are we gonna do?

598
01:05:48.141 --> 01:05:50.497
I say we go and talk
to a man about a horse.

599
01:05:50.577 --> 01:05:52.617
Did you hit your head or something?
You're babbling.

600
01:05:52.697 --> 01:05:55.535
A Trojan horse, Boston. Come on!

601
01:05:58.317 --> 01:06:00.789
Over here, you wanker!

602
01:06:03.289 --> 01:06:06.612
You are puny and disrespectful.

603
01:06:06.692 --> 01:06:09.330
Let me see your madness.

604
01:06:15.953 --> 01:06:18.775
Well, that's the trouble with someone
like me. Been there, done that.

605
01:06:18.855 --> 01:06:22.229
I shall make you beg for death.

606
01:06:22.309 --> 01:06:24.897
Can I beg you to stop talking?

607
01:06:24.977 --> 01:06:28.035
I mean, all wizards are touched,
but you, you're a full-blown nutter.

608
01:06:28.115 --> 01:06:32.005
I will tear your soul apart.

609
01:06:32.085 --> 01:06:34.641
And what happened
to not prattling with mortals?

610
01:06:34.721 --> 01:06:37.793
You chatter like my grandma
at a book club.

611
01:06:38.726 --> 01:06:40.646
Now, Boston!

612
01:06:40.726 --> 01:06:43.001
Trick or treat, freak!

613
01:07:02.114 --> 01:07:05.420
Is that a sword in your chest,
or are you just glad to see me?

614
01:07:06.453 --> 01:07:08.542
Merlin sends his regards.

615
01:07:09.570 --> 01:07:12.361
And by the way, you lose.

616
01:07:33.380 --> 01:07:35.617
I don't think so.

617
01:07:53.868 --> 01:07:57.222
Johnny, I was... I was under a compulsion.

618
01:07:57.302 --> 01:08:01.896
You've got to save me.
You owe me. You owe me!

619
01:08:02.076 --> 01:08:06.849
Sorry, mate. Can't take the chance
that Destiny is still pulling your strings.

620
01:08:08.214 --> 01:08:11.222
John, please! Help me!

621
01:08:18.125 --> 01:08:21.181
Help me, you bastard!

622
01:08:21.661 --> 01:08:23.900
Help me!

623
01:08:25.464 --> 01:08:27.687
That was unpleasant.

624
01:08:28.167 --> 01:08:30.190
What the hell did I miss?

625
01:08:30.270 --> 01:08:33.143
Z, you're okay. I thought...

626
01:08:33.223 --> 01:08:36.428
My head feels like
the morning after Brixton.

627
01:08:37.610 --> 01:08:39.848
Surely not that bad.

628
01:08:40.713 --> 01:08:44.605
So Merlin's spell hath ended.

629
01:08:44.685 --> 01:08:46.640
It would seem so.

630
01:08:46.720 --> 01:08:50.592
Though it's a "good news,
bad news" sort of thing.

631
01:09:01.668 --> 01:09:04.690
- What's going on?
- Yeah. He wasn't wounded.

632
01:09:04.770 --> 01:09:09.277
Unless I miss my guess, that happened
on the day he was bound to Etrigan.

633
01:09:10.910 --> 01:09:13.166
And now that I'm not...

634
01:09:13.246 --> 01:09:15.836
I'm truly sorry, Jason.

635
01:09:15.916 --> 01:09:19.955
Don't be. It's a welcome end.

636
01:09:31.465 --> 01:09:35.856
For 500 years, he and I have been bound.

637
01:09:35.936 --> 01:09:40.292
A demon from hell, a knight of renown.

638
01:09:40.372 --> 01:09:44.130
Though we were cursed
to be slaves to each other,

639
01:09:44.210 --> 01:09:48.402
I know of no man
I'd want more for a brother.

640
01:09:48.482 --> 01:09:50.759
Farewell, mortal.

641
01:10:05.931 --> 01:10:08.322
You couldn't have picked a better place.

642
01:10:08.602 --> 01:10:11.157
The village where he was born
was over there.

643
01:10:11.237 --> 01:10:13.608
Too bad it took this to get him home.

644
01:10:15.075 --> 01:10:18.280
Batman asked me to be
in the Justice League.

645
01:10:18.662 --> 01:10:19.816
And you're considering it?

646
01:10:19.896 --> 01:10:22.903
I visited their headquarters
a few days ago.

647
01:10:22.983 --> 01:10:25.671
It's interesting, and like you said,

648
01:10:25.751 --> 01:10:28.208
maybe it's time to make a difference.

649
01:10:28.688 --> 01:10:30.546
Listening to me now?

650
01:10:30.856 --> 01:10:33.027
They want you, too.

651
01:10:34.662 --> 01:10:37.966
Good one, Z. Too right, they do.

652
01:10:40.566 --> 01:10:42.699
You have got to be bloody kidding.

653
01:10:42.779 --> 01:10:45.493
No way. Batty would go mental.

654
01:10:45.573 --> 01:10:47.678
He was the one who asked,

655
01:10:47.758 --> 01:10:50.662
and I told him that's what you'd say.

656
01:10:53.045 --> 01:10:54.882
Be safe, John.

657
01:11:07.961 --> 01:11:10.283
Now, hold on. Hold on.

658
01:11:10.363 --> 01:11:12.318
Maybe I've been a bit rash.

659
01:11:12.398 --> 01:11:14.803
Could you tell me more over a drink?

660
01:11:15.836 --> 01:11:18.624
We could rechristen the House, as it were.

661
01:11:19.071 --> 01:11:22.607
- A drink?
- Yeah, a drink.

662
01:11:26.112 --> 01:11:30.169
Don't think this is gonna turn into
some sort of Manchester weekend.

663
01:11:30.249 --> 01:11:32.639
Get that out of your head.

664
01:11:32.919 --> 01:11:35.609
We could have a Trewhiddle Tuesday.

665
01:11:36.489 --> 01:11:40.495
- No, definitely not.
- Well, let's mark that as a maybe.

666
01:11:58.845 --> 01:12:02.317
Now, that's what I call
making yourself useful, love.
